{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>As complainers.</b> From the root און and עמל, like מחשבות אונך." "<b>And HaShem heard.</b> That they spoke words of און." "<b>And fire burned among them.</b> Measure for measure: because they transgressed and gazed at the appearance of the glory of the Shekhinah, which is like consuming fire, and they had been warned against this at Sinai — by that same thing they were punished here. This refers to the leaders of the people, as Rashi explained in the portion of Mishpatim, regarding ויראו את אלקי ישראל." "<b>And it consumed the edge of the camp.</b> Therefore ויצעק העם אל משה — they feared lest it spread through the entire camp."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:27.449229341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}